          "author_email": "530235+brandon-fryslie@users.noreply.github.com",
          "timestamp": "2026-10-16T21:26:19-06:00",
          "message": "Markdown draws an autolink as Rich does, and makes every link's href as markdown-it does (rich-unfiled-791c.95jg)\n\n`<http://e.com>` and `<a@b.co>` now draw as links whose text is the address,\nan email linking to mailto:. Links, images and autolinks all take their href\nfrom src/renderables/markdown-url.ts, a port of markdown-it-py's\nnormalizeLink / normalizeLinkText / validateLink with the mdurl and punycode\npieces they stand on — so a javascript:, vbscript:, file: or non-image data:\nURL is no link, as in Rich. Tests pinned against Rich 14 output.\n"
        }
      ]
